<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" article-type="correction"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">J Cell Biol</journal-id><journal-title>The Journal of Cell Biology</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">0021-9525</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1540-8140</issn><publisher><publisher-name>The Rockefeller University Press</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2150889</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="publisher-id">15562</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1083/jcb.200111191545961cor</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Correction</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>Correction</article-title></title-group><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><day>10</day><month>12</month><year>2001</year></pub-date><volume>155</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>1083</fpage><lpage>1083</lpage><permissions><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9; 2001, The Rockefeller University Press</copyright-statement></permissions></article-meta></front><body><p><related-article related-article-type="corrected-article" vol="154" page="961" id="N0x199fa80N0x1ebb080" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="11524434" ext-link-type="pubmed">Nakamura et al. Vol. 154, No. 5, September 3, 2001. Pages 961&#x02013;972.</related-article></p><p>In the Results on page 965, parts of two successive sentences were mistakenly omitted. The incorrect sentence reads &#x0201c;Western blot analysis of types 1, 2, and 3 of the InsP<sub>3</sub>R revealed that these cells contain all three types of InsP<sub>3</sub>R at a ratio of 10:70:20 (Fig. 6).&#x0201d; The correct text and its respective reference appears below. This does not affect the conclusion of the work.</p><p>Western blot analysis of types 1, 2, and 3 of the InsP<sub>3</sub>R revealed that these cells express at the protein level significant amounts of each isoform (Fig. 6). An exact quantification was performed by direct comparison of the levels in each cell line with those measured in RBL-2H3 cells, which contain all three types of InsP<sub>3</sub>R at a ratio of 10:70:20 (Wilson et al., 1998).</p><p>Wilson, B.S., J.R. Pfeiffer, A.J. Smith, J.M. Oliver, J.A. Oberdorf, and R.J. Wojcikiewicz. 1998. Calcium-dependent clustering of inositol 1,4,5-triphosphate receptors. <italic>Mol. Biol. Cell</italic>. 9:1465&#x02013;1478.</p></body></article>